---
layout: base.njk
title: "DPRK Hunting"
description: "A filterable library of threat hunts for DPRK IT-worker fraud and Contagious Interview activity, with Sigma, Splunk SPL, Microsoft Defender and Sentinel KQL, CrowdStrike, Cortex XQL, Elastic, osquery and YARA queries on each hunt's own page."
permalink: "/hunts/"
extra_head: '<script src="/assets/js/hunt-filter.js" defer></script>'
---
{#
  src/hunts/index.njk: a tile per entry in src/_data/hunts/hunts.json, each
  linking to /hunts/{id}/ (hunt-page.njk). Loops iterate `hunts.hunts`. Facet
  chips (type, query technology, and OS from `platforms`) are derived from the
  data, so a new value adds a chip.
#}
<section>
  <h1>DPRK Hunting</h1>
  <p>
    Threat hunts for the DPRK remote IT-worker scheme and the "Contagious
    Interview" fake-recruiter campaign. Each hunt states what it detects, lists
    the indicators it matches on, and carries copy-paste queries.
  </p>
  <p>
    A query marked as reproduced is as the cited source wrote it; one marked as
    written for this site was composed against reported indicators. None is a
    vendor-supported detection.
  </p>

  {% set disclaimer = {
    title: "Tuning required before use",
    body: 'Adapt each query to your schema and tune it against the false positives noted on the hunt. Address and domain indicators go stale as operators rotate hosts.'
  } %}{% include "partials/disclaimer.njk" %}
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Hunt library</h2>

  {# The chip bar is `hidden` in the markup and revealed by hunt-filter.js, the
     same progressive-enhancement pattern as the /sources/ filter: without
     JavaScript these buttons — and the sort <select> alongside them — stay
     hidden rather than rendering as dead controls, so a reader without
     JavaScript gets the full grid in library order. The count sits outside
     the bar so it is still shown in that case. #}
  {# Hidden and revealed by the same script, for the same reason as the chips
     below it. Searching reaches into each hunt's indicator table as well as
     its title and summary, so an artefact name finds the hunt that matches on
     it — see the data-search attribute in partials/hunt-card.njk. #}
  <div class="table-filter" data-hunt-search hidden>
    {% set searchBox = { id: "hunt-search-input", label: "Search hunts", placeholder: "Title, what it detects, or an indicator such as NetKey or Astrill", attr: "data-hunt-search-input", count: "data-hunt-count", countText: (hunts.hunts.length + " hunts.") } %}{% include "partials/search-box.njk" %}
  </div>


  <div data-hunt-filter hidden>
    {% set filterChips = { dimension: "type", label: "Filter by hunt type", short: "Type", allLabel: "All types (" + (hunts.hunts.length) + ")", counts: hunts.hunts | countBy("hunt_type") } %}{% include "partials/filter-chips.njk" %}
    {% set filterChips = { dimension: "os", label: "Filter by operating system or log plane", short: "OS", allLabel: "All platforms (" + (hunts.hunts.length) + ")", counts: hunts.hunts | countValues("platforms") } %}{% include "partials/filter-chips.njk" %}
    {% set filterChips = { dimension: "platform", label: "Filter by query language", short: "Query language", allLabel: "All query languages (" + (hunts.hunts.length) + ")", counts: hunts.hunts | countDistinctIn("queries", "platform") } %}{% include "partials/filter-chips.njk" %}
    <select data-hunt-sort aria-label="Sort hunts by" data-short-label="Sort">
      <option value="default">Best match</option>
      <option value="type">Hunt type</option>
      <option value="platform">Query language</option>
    </select>
  </div>

  {% set resultTools = { target: "[data-hunt-grid]", noun: "hunts" } %}{% include "partials/result-tools.njk" %}

  <ul class="hunt-grid" data-hunt-grid>
    {% for entry in hunts.hunts %}{% set cardHunt = entry %}{% include "partials/hunt-card.njk" %}{% endfor %}
  </ul>

  <p data-hunt-empty hidden role="status" aria-live="polite"><em>No hunt matches that search and filter combination.</em></p>
</section>
